Package: @PACKAGE@
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: gnome-shell (>= 48), systemd
Recommends: gnome-shell-extension-prefs
Section: gnome
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/itowhid06/gnome-auto-shutdown
Description: GNOME Shell extension to shut down the computer on a timer
 Auto Shutdown adds a menu to the GNOME top bar for scheduling an automatic
 power off: after 10, 30 or 60 minutes, after any custom number of hours and
 minutes, or at a specific time of day. It shows a countdown in the top bar
 and warns with a notification before the deadline, with options to postpone
 or cancel.
 .
 The timer is held by systemd-logind, so it keeps running when the screen is
 locked or GNOME Shell restarts, and it is the same schedule used by
 "shutdown +N".
